==English==
===Etymology===
[[poly-]] + [[domino|(d)omino]], as if the ''d'' were for [[di-]], two, a domino being made up of two squares

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|polyominoes}}

#{{geometry}} A [[polyform]] made by joining one or more [[square]]s edge to edge in various [[arrangement]]s.

====Synonyms====
*[[n-omino|''n''-omino]]

====Related terms====
*[[decomino]] (10 squares)
*[[dodecomino]] (12 squares)
*[[domino]] (2 squares)
*[[heptomino]] (7 squares)
*[[hexomino]] (6 squares)
*[[monomino]] (1 square)
*[[nonomino]] (9 squares)
*[[octomino]] (8 squares)
*[[pentomino]] (5 squares) 
*[[tetromino]] (4 squares)
*[[triomino]], [[tromino]] (3 squares)
*[[undecomino]] (11 squares)

